# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# BYLINE ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
# Copy this file to .env and fill in your values
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── Required for AI generation ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Anthropic API key (used when users run on credits, not their own key)
# https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# ── Required for payments ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Stripe secret key
# https://dashboard.stripe.com/apikeys
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_...

# Stripe webhook secret (for production webhook verification)
# https://dashboard.stripe.com/webhooks
# Create endpoint: https://yourdomain.com/api/webhook/stripe
# Events to listen for: checkout.session.completed, charge.refunded
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_...

# ── Required for user accounts ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Supabase project URL and keys
# https://supabase.com/dashboard/project/_/settings/api
SUPABASE_URL=https://xxx.supabase.co
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJ...
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=eyJ...

# ── Required for session storage (production) ──────────────────────────────────
# Vercel KV / Upstash Redis
# Auto-injected by Vercel when you connect a KV store in the dashboard
# For local dev with KV, copy from Vercel project settings → Storage
# Without these, the app uses in-memory store (resets on restart)
KV_REST_API_URL=https://...
KV_REST_API_TOKEN=...

# ── Optional: Analytics ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PostHog API key for product analytics
# https://posthog.com/docs/libraries/node
POSTHOG_API_KEY=phc_...
POSTHOG_HOST=https://us.i.posthog.com

# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# SUPABASE SETUP INSTRUCTIONS
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# 1. Create a new Supabase project at https://supabase.com
#
# 2. Run the migration in supabase/migrations/20261029000000_initial_schema.sql
#    - Go to SQL Editor in your Supabase dashboard
#    - Paste and run the migration file contents
#
# 3. Enable authentication providers:
#    - Go to Authentication → Providers
#    - Enable "Email" (magic link is enabled by default)
#    - Enable "Google" and configure OAuth credentials:
#      https://supabase.com/docs/guides/auth/social-login/auth-google
#
# 4. Set up redirect URLs:
#    - Go to Authentication → URL Configuration
#    - Add your production URL to "Redirect URLs": https://yourdomain.com/app
#    - For local dev, also add: http://localhost:3000/app
#
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# STRIPE WEBHOOK SETUP
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# 1. Go to https://dashboard.stripe.com/webhooks
# 2. Click "Add endpoint"
# 3. Endpoint URL: https://yourdomain.com/api/webhook/stripe
# 4. Select events:
#    - checkout.session.completed
#    - charge.refunded
# 5. Copy the signing secret to STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET
#
# For local development:
# 1. Install Stripe CLI: https://stripe.com/docs/stripe-cli
# 2. Run: stripe listen --forward-to localhost:3000/api/webhook/stripe
# 3. Use the webhook signing secret it provides
#
